{"name":"Pretty Maiden","hex":"#849457","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pretty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pleasant to the sight or other senses; attractive, especially of women or children. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of objects or things: nice-looking, appealing."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Somewhat, fairly, quite; sometimes also (by meiosis) very.","Prettily, in a pretty manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty"},{"term":"maiden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A girl or an unmarried young woman.","A female virgin."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Virgin.","Without offspring."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maiden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Virginity","blocks":[{"text":"Virginity is a social construct that denotes the state of a person who has never engaged in sexual intercourse. As it is not an objective term with an operational definition, social definitions of what constitutes virginity, or the lack thereof, vary. Heterosexual individuals may or may not consider loss of virginity to occur only through penile–vaginal penetration, while people of other sexual orientations often include oral sex, anal sex, or manual sex in their definitions of virginity loss. The term \"virgin\" encompasses a range of definitions, as found in traditional, modern, and ethical concepts. Religious rituals for regaining virginity exist in many cultures. Some men and women who practice celibacy after losing their virginity consider themselves born-again virgins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg/330px-William-Adolphe_Bouguereau_%281825-1905%29_-Youth_%281893%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virginity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu